                            <comment id="16552854" author="slukyanov" created="Mon, 23 Jul 2018 13:23:46 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Test idea: create a custom POJO like &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
    &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;class &lt;/span&gt;Foo &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;implements&lt;/span&gt; Serializable, Binarylizable {
        writeObject() { &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; Exception(); }
        readObject() { &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; Exception(); }
        writeBinary() { &lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;/* actual marshalling */&lt;/span&gt; }
        readBinary() { &lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;/* actual marshalling */&lt;/span&gt; }
    }
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;and use it in the queries. Ignite should never use writeObject()/readObject() if a class is Binarylizable, so if something is wrong we&apos;ll see the exceptions.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
